martha-engine
=============

martha-engine is the agent engine that ships with Martha. It is a modified
version of goose (https://github.com/aaif-goose/goose), copyright the goose
authors, licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0. The licence text is
in LICENSE.

martha-engine is not goose and is not endorsed by the goose project or its
maintainers. The name goose appears here only to say where this work comes
from.

## Changes

Each change is one commit on top of upstream goose, so the whole difference
can be read in one place.

- The command-line binary is named martha-engine instead of goose.
- The engine keeps its own state under its own name: its configuration,
  data, state and cache folders, the system-wide configuration, the OS
  keyring service and its global checks and plugin settings. It never
  writes a goose installation's folders or secrets.
- What it still reads under goose's name, on purpose:
  - The shared agent folders that several agents use, as goose does:
    .goose/agents, .goose/recipes and .goose/skills in the project,
    ~/.goose/agents and ~/.goose/recipes in your home folder, a project's
    .config/goose plugin settings, and project memories in .goose/memory,
    which the memory extension also writes.
  - An import from goose, only when an ACP client asks for one during
    onboarding: it reads ~/.config/goose/config.yaml (provider, model,
    extensions), the secrets.yaml beside it and its skills, and copies them
    into the engine's own configuration. It changes nothing in goose's folder.
- --version, the usage line, the info header and the engine's own HTTP user
  agents name martha-engine, and --version says it is built on Goose.
- Telemetry is compiled out: the telemetry feature is not part of the default
  or portable-default builds, so the engine contains no usage-event sender
  and does not ask about telemetry.
- Self-update is compiled out: the update feature is not part of the default
  build, so the engine has no update command. Martha's installer is the only
  thing that changes what is installed.
- The fork's own checks of these changes live in martha/checks.
